      "hints": [
        "Undo the natural logarithm in \\(\\ln(1+e^{-3x})=2\\) by exponentiating both sides.",
        "Isolate \\(e^{-3x}\\) as \\(e^2-1\\), which is positive.",
        "Take logarithms again to solve for \\(x\\), then round only the resulting value to 3 decimal places."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "State the given logarithmic equation:\n$$\\ln(1 + \\mathrm{e}^{-3x}) = 2$$",
        "Exponentiate both sides with base $\\mathrm{e}$ to remove the natural logarithm:\n$$\\mathrm{e}^{\\ln(1 + \\mathrm{e}^{-3x})} = \\mathrm{e}^2$$\n$$1 + \\mathrm{e}^{-3x} = \\mathrm{e}^2$$",
        "Subtract $1$ from both sides to isolate the exponential term $\\mathrm{e}^{-3x}$:\n$$\\mathrm{e}^{-3x} = \\mathrm{e}^2 - 1$$",
        "Evaluate the numerical value of $\\mathrm{e}^2 - 1$:\n$$\\mathrm{e}^2 \\approx 7.389056 \\implies \\mathrm{e}^2 - 1 \\approx 6.389056 > 0$$",
        "Take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n$$\\ln(\\mathrm{e}^{-3x}) = \\ln(\\mathrm{e}^2 - 1)$$\n$$-3x = \\ln(\\mathrm{e}^2 - 1)$$",
        "Divide by $-3$ to solve explicitly for $x$:\n$$x = -\\dfrac{1}{3}\\ln(\\mathrm{e}^2 - 1)$$",
        "Evaluate the numerical value:\n$$\\ln(6.389056) \\approx 1.854587$$\n$$x = -\\dfrac{1.854587}{3} \\approx -0.618196$$",
        "Round the answer to $3$ decimal places:\n$$x = -0.618$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
